 {
  "id": "3988284223643830835",
  "type": "Sidecar",
  "shortCode": "DdZO17dlcoz",
  "caption": "“Before I started playing hockey at the age of 6 years old I fell in love with the gear and the sport. Almost every night I wanted to play street or ice hockey and asked my dad or brother to shoot at me. Since we were not allowed to use pucks in our house, I made a ball out of paper and had my dad throw it at me while he was watching tv. I loved the goalie gear but after a couple of years I realized quickly that skating around the ice and scoring goals is way more fun. Little did I know back then that one day. I can make a living doing what I love. Hockey has given and is still giving me more than I could have ever imagined. I travelled the world, formed meaningful relationships, experienced setbacks, won medals, but most importantly, I found a place I love to invest my time into.”\n\nThank you so much @alinamueller_ for choosing to become a Pixelle and for sharing your journey into playing professional hockey. It’s such an inspiring story 💜🏒\n\n#Pixelle #GirlsInHockey #WomensHockey #GirlsWhoPlay #LetHerPlay",
